{"type":"text","timestamp":1787503885356,"sessionID":"ses_fd07aa253ffeA65EQl88ShiV73","part":{"id":"prt_02f88a47f0012nEAEErR5XSX4H","messageID":"msg_02f888dd0001a1ETaioTQhyIs4","sessionID":"ses_fd07aa253ffeA65EQl88ShiV73","type":"text","text":"All 12 tests pass. The implementation is complete — here's the summary:\n\n## Implementation\n\n**`run-explorer.mjs`** — kept `sampleRuns` untouched and implemented the three pure exports plus the browser layer:\n- `filterRuns` throws `TypeError` for non-arrays, treats `\"all\"` as a disabled filter, matches exactly (case-sensitive), and returns a new array via `.filter()`.\n- `sortRuns` throws `TypeError` for non-arrays and unsupported orders, sorts a spread copy with comparator chains implementing the full tie-break sequences (`score-desc`, `time-asc`, `cost-asc` with `null` costs last), using a deterministic codepoint `id` comparison.\n- `summarizeRuns` returns exactly the five required keys, computes pass rate rounded to one decimal, median over a numerically sorted copy (averaging the middle pair for even counts), and accumulates costs as integer cents (`0.1 + 0.2 → 0.3`, no FP residue). Empty input yields all zeros.\n- DOM code is guarded by `typeof document !== \"undefined\"` so Node test imports stay side-effect free. Cards are built exclusively with `createElement`/`textContent`, the list is cleared with `replaceChildren()` (no `innerHTML` anywhere), and each `change` on any select re-renders records, summaries, and the live status. Reset restores `all`/`all`/`score-desc`.\n\n**`index.html`** — semantic layout: one `<h1>`, a lede stating these are sample records, not final study results; labeled native selects with the exact required IDs/options; `Reset filters` button; four `<output>` summary values (`visible-count`, `pass-rate`, `median-time`, `known-cost`) with a note that unknown subscription costs are excluded; `role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"` result-count region; initially `hidden` `empty-state`.\n\n**`styles.css`** — card-based visual hierarchy (intro → filter panel → summary grid → result grid), fluid grids that use horizontal space at desktop and collapse to stacked, scroll-free layouts via `@media (max-width: 720px)`, hover states on controls/cards, `:focus-visible` outlines, high-contrast Pass/Fail badges with visible text (not color alone), and a `prefers-reduced-motion` rule.\n\n## Added edge cases (`student-tests.mjs`, 8 tests)\n\nNon-array `TypeError`s for all three functions; case-sensitive matching (`\"codex\"` matches nothing); `\"all\"` returning a new array; unsupported/empty/undefined sort orders; `time-asc` tie-breaking by score then `id`; `cost-asc` nulls-last ordering with score tie-break among nulls; all-zero summary for `[]`; even-count median averaging; FP-safe cost totaling with one-decimal pass-rate rounding (33.3%); and a composition test over the seeded `sampleRuns`. No skips, todos, or placeholders.\n\n## Test result\n\n`node --test benchmark/fixtures/T4-run-explorer/run-explorer.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T4-run-explorer/student-tests.mjs` → **12 pass, 0 fail** (4 committed + 8 added). Only the four allowed files were modified; the committed suite is untouched.\n\n## Browser behavior not directly verified\n\nThis environment has no browser, so I could not visually confirm: responsive reflow at ≤720 px, select/reset interactivity and `aria-live` announcements, hover/focus-visible rendering, reduced-motion behavior, or the empty state appearing (reachable via Codex + Fail). These are implemented per contract but warrant the external browser QA pass.","time":{"start":1787503879295,"end":1787503885354}}}
